Marlene Dietrich (born December 27, 1901, Schöneberg [now in Berlin], Germany—died May 6, 1992, 
Paris, France) was a German American motion-picture actress whose beauty, voice, 
aura of sophistication, and languid sensuality made her one of the world’s most glamorous 
film stars.

