					"text" : "Hollywood was laid out as a subdivision in 1887 by Harvey Wilcox, who was a <a href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/topic\/prohibition-alcohol-interdict\">prohibitionist<\/a> from Kansas. However, real-estate magnate H.J. Whitley transformed Hollywood into a wealthy and popular residential area. Hollywood became a municipality in 1903 and was incorporated into <a href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/place\/Los-Angeles-California\">Los Angeles<\/a> in 1910."
